## Per the request ("add floating test SL outcome for test in the
## fields for attacker/defender(if opposed)"): the most recent opposed
## test's own result, floated as a pair of small +N/-N chips between
## the Attacker/Defender boxes — green for whichever side won the
## opposition, red for whichever lost. Only ever set from an actually
## OPPOSED test (a melee attack's Attack-vs-Defence roll, or a Trick/
## Batter-style opposed action) — an unopposed ranged shot at a flat
## Target Number clears it instead, same as a fresh turn/new target
## (see _refresh_enemy_display, which only renders these chips while
## "attacker"/"defender" here still match who's currently shown in the
## strip, so a stale result never lingers onto an unrelated pairing).
var _last_opposed_sl_result: Dictionary = {}

## Shared by _show_attack_cards (melee/ranged attacks) and
## _show_opposed_action_cards (Trick/Batter/etc.) — both already
## compute exactly these five things for their own roll cards, so this
## just captures them for the top-strip chips too instead of
## recomputing anything.
func _record_opposed_sl_result(actor: Character, actor_test: TestResolver.TestResult, actor_won: bool,
		opponent: Character, opponent_test: TestResolver.TestResult, opponent_won: bool) -> void:
	_last_opposed_sl_result = {
		"attacker": actor,
		"attacker_sl": actor_test.success_levels if actor_test != null else 0,
		"attacker_won": actor_won,
		"defender": opponent,
		"defender_sl": opponent_test.success_levels if opponent_test != null else 0,
		"defender_won": opponent_won,
	}
	_refresh_enemy_display()

## An unopposed action (a ranged shot with no real Defence test, or any
## other single-roll action) explicitly clears the chips rather than
## leaving a stale opposed result floating over an exchange that never
## happened — called from the same sites _record_opposed_sl_result
## would otherwise be called from, whenever that particular result
## turns out not to have been opposed after all.
func _clear_opposed_sl_result() -> void:
	if _last_opposed_sl_result.is_empty():
		return
	_last_opposed_sl_result = {}
	_refresh_enemy_display()

